Rule 1 (input tensor must be at least 2-D)
{v_1: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (axis indices must be within valid range [-ndim, ndim-1])
{v_1: tensor, v_3: int, v_4: int} |= 0 - ndim(v_1) ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1 ∧ 0 - ndim(v_1) ≤ v_4 ∧ v_4 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 3 (axis1 and axis2 must be different)
{v_3: int, v_4: int} |= v_3 ≠ v_4
>>
Rule 4 (dtype must be a valid dtype object; suppresses “Cannot interpret 'torch.int64' as a data type”)
{v_1: tensor, v_5: dtype} |= v_5 = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (nonempty diagonal when using nonnegative axes)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int, v_3: int, v_4: int} |= v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) ∧ v_4 < ndim(v_1) ∧ v_3 ≠ v_4 ∧ if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 < shape(v_1, v_4) else 0 - v_2 < shape(v_1, v_3)
>>
Rule 6 (each dimension size is nonnegative)
{v_1: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
